Why do we need it?
If Lambda cannot process Kinesis records—for example, because DynamoDB is unavailable—it retries. After the configured retry or record-age limit is reached, its Kinesis event-source mapping can send failure information to this queue.
The eventual connections will be:

Success: Kinesis → Lambda → DynamoDB
Exhausted processing failure: Kinesis event-source mapping → SQS failure queue

Important: this SQS destination receives failure metadata, not the complete original payment records. Recovering the original records depends on them still being available in Kinesis.



